[Opening "Vienna Game: Vienna Gambit, Accepted"]
[ChapterName "Vienna Gambit — Accepted 3...exf4"]
[ChapterIndex "2"]

1. e4 {White controls central territory.} 1... e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. f4! exf4?! {A dubious positional surrender. Giving up e5 enables White to push e5 with decisive tempo.} 4. e5! {The thematic punch! Evicting Black's best developed piece.} 4... Qe7 {Pinning the e-pawn along the e-file.} (4... Ne4 5. Nxe4 Qh4+ 6. Nf2 Bc5 7. d4 Bb6 8. Nf3 Qe7 9. Bxf4 {White wins a piece and retains a decisive central superiority.}) (4... Nd5 5. Nxd5 Qh4+ 6. Ke2! f3+ 7. Nxf3 Qe4+ 8. Ne3 {White safely shelters the king with an overwhelming material advantage.}) 5. Qe2 {Unpinning the e-pawn while forcing Black's knight to retreat all the way back home.} 5... Ng8 6. Nf3 {Developing with tempo, controlling d4 and preparing to recapture the f4 pawn.} 6... d6 7. d4 dxe5 8. dxe5 c6 9. Bxf4 {White has regained the gambit pawn with an enormous developmental lead.} 9... Bg4 10. O-O-O Nd7 11. Ne4! {Dominating the board with lethal threats like Nd6+ or Nd5.} *

