1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. f4! Nc6?! {A common tactical mistake at club level, misjudging the central pawn structure.} 4. fxe5! Nxe5 5. d4! {Seizing complete central dominance with tempo on the knight.} 5... Nc6 (5... Ng6 6. e5 Ng8 7. Nf3 Bb4 8. Bc4 d5 9. exd6 Qxd6 10. O-O {White achieves a winning initiative.}) 6. e5! {Driving the other black knight back into retreat as well.} 6... Ng8 7. Nf3 d5 8. Bd3 Bg4 9. Be3 Bb4 10. O-O Nge7 11. Ne2! {White consolidates the central pawn roller and prepares c3 and d5 to blast open Black's king.} *

