1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nf6 3. f4! d6?! {A passive choice transposing into a cramped Philidor Defense structure.} 4. Nf3! Bg4 (4... Nbd7 5. Bc4 Be7 6. d3 O-O 7. O-O c6 8. a4 {White controls more space on both flanks.}) (4... exf4 5. d4 Bg4 6. Bxf4 Be7 7. Bc4 {White commands the open center.}) 5. h3! {Challenging the pin immediately.} 5... Bxf3 6. Qxf3 Nc6 7. Bb5 a6 8. Bxc6+ bxc6 9. d3 Be7 10. O-O O-O 11. f5! {White closes the center to prepare an unstoppable kingside avalanche with g4-g5.} *

