[Opening "Vienna Game: Max Lange Defense, Hamppe-Paulsen Attack"]
[ChapterName "Vienna Copycat — 3...Bc5 & 4.Qg4!"]
[ChapterIndex "5"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Bc5 {The Copycat variation. Black mirrors White's bishop placement.} 4. Qg4! {The venomous Hamppe-Paulsen Queen attack! White strikes at g7 and tests Black's tactical awareness.} 4... Qf6 (4... g6 5. Qf3 Nf6 6. Nge2 d6 7. d3 Bg4 8. Qg3 h6 9. O-O Qd7 10. h3 {White retains harmonious development and attacking lines.}) (4... Kf8 5. Qf3 Nf6 6. Nge2 d6 7. d3 Bg4 8. Qg3 h6 9. O-O {Black has surrendered castling rights permanently.}) 5. Nd5! {The brilliant counter-sacrifice, allowing Qxf2+ to trap and crush the black queen.} 5... Qxf2+ 6. Kd1 Kf8 7. Nh3 Qd4 8. d3! {Defending the bishop and preparing to snare the trapped black queen with c3.} 8... Bb6 9. c3 Qc5 10. Rf1! d6 11. Qf3 Be6 12. Ng5! {Black's position collapses under the relentless assault on f7.} *

