[Opening "Vienna Game: Vienna Hybrid, Italian Setup"]
[ChapterName "Vienna Hybrid — 3...Nf6 & 4.d3"]
[ChapterIndex "6"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. d3! {The Vienna Hybrid. Solidifying the center and keeping the option of f2-f4 in reserve without allowing tactical counter-punches.} 4... Bc5 (4... Bb4 5. Ne2 d5 6. exd5 Nxd5 7. O-O Be6 8. Bxd5 Bxd5 9. Nxd5 Qxd5 10. c3 {White secures the bishop pair and solid center.}) (4... Na5 5. Nge2 Nxc4 6. dxc4 Bc5 7. Qd3 d6 8. O-O O-O 9. Bg5 {White neutralizes Black's knight sortie with rapid piece coordination.}) 5. f4! {Thematic breakthrough! The f-file opens while the c4 bishop applies diagonal pressure on f7.} 5... d6 6. Nf3 a6 7. f5! {Locking the center and launching kingside operations with Bg5 and Nd5.} 7... h6 8. a3 b5 9. Ba2 Bb7 10. Nd5! Nxd5 11. Bxd5 {White exerts permanent diagonal strangulation and prepares kingside piece penetration.} *

